course: dictionary
lesson: 8027
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning is used. Reformation comes from re- (again) and form (shape), so it means putting something back into a better shape. «In the 1500s reformers such as Martin Luther protested against problems in the Catholic Church, and the Protestant churches grew from this Reformation.» Church, reformers and protested are the clues, so this is a history word.
explain: A capital letter is a clue too. The Reformation, with a capital R, names one big event in history. «The Reformation split western Christianity into Catholic and Protestant churches.» Here it means the time when some Christians broke away and started Protestant churches.
explain: With a small letter, a reformation can mean a big change that makes something better, especially a person's behaviour. «Ben's reformation» would mean Ben changed his bad ways. To check, swap in "a big change for the better" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: The Reformation is a time in history, about five hundred years ago, when some Christians broke away from the Roman Catholic Church.
fact: The Reformation led to the Protestant churches, which is why there are Catholic and Protestant churches today.
fact: Martin Luther is one of the reformers who protested against problems in the Catholic Church in the 1500s.
fact: A reformation with a small r can mean a big change that makes something better, such as «a reformation of character».
fact: Re- at the start of a word often means again, as in reform, which means to put something right again.
exercise: «In the 1500s reformers such as Martin Luther protested against problems in the Catholic Church.» What does the Reformation name? | *A time in history when some Christians broke away and started Protestant churches | A school for teaching church music | A summer holiday in Europe | A new type of castle
exercise: «Ben's reformation was amazing: he stopped lying and started helping at home.» What does reformation mean here? | A trip to the seaside | *A big change for the better in how Ben behaves | A loud argument with his family | A new kind of bread
exercise: The word reform is inside reformation. What does re- usually mean? | Under | Away | Very big | *Again
test: What is the Reformation? | *A time in history when Christians broke away from the Catholic Church and started Protestant churches | A kind of church building with a tall tower | A holiday for families in the spring
test: «A complete reformation» could describe what? | *A total change that makes something much better | A mistake that is easy to fix | A quiet walk in the park | A small crack in a wall
exam: Lily says the Reformation is just a old school building. Why is she wrong? | Because the Reformation is a kind of castle | Because the Reformation is a type of music played in churches | *Because the Reformation was a time in history when some Christians broke away and started Protestant churches | Because the Reformation is only a word for a holiday
